  "description": "ESA says its Euclid space telescope, built to study dark energy and galaxies, has found a previously unknown comet in images taken on September 16 to 24, 2026. The Minor Planet Center confirmed it as comet C/2026 S1 (Euclid) on October 8. It is about 1.3 billion km from Earth; ESA says it is not a target for the Comet Interceptor mission.\n\nSources: ESA release (Oct 2026); Universe Today; Sci.News; Minor Planet Center.\n\n#science #space #comet #euclid",
